WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.670
-Three children, 8, 3 and then
one that´s very young, yeah?

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.138
-Yes, Eli is 1-years-Old.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations on that.
-Yes.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
I say I have two children
and a terrorist.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Who´s the terrorist?
-The middle child, of course.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:12.912
-The middle one´s the terrorist?
-Yes, yes.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.
That´s interesting to know.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:18.284
Do the -- so the 8 and 3 --
obviously one has no idea,

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.920
do the 8 and 3 year old have any
sense of what you do?

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The 8-year-old does, yes.
-Okay.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.958
Impressed with it at all?

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.760
-I think she is, actually.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that´s good.
-Yeah.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.830
-Does she understand how hard it
is to do three-hundred episodes

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.332 size:78% position:39%
of a television show?
-That, she definitely

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:33.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
doesn´t know.
-Yeah.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Not many people do.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
And congratulations on that.

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-Did you have any --

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:41.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
At what point in
the run did you ever --

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
have comprehended
it could go on this long?

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.912
-Well, every year I keep saying
this is the last year,

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
they´re definitely going
to get sick of us.

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:49.582
The ratings are going to plummet

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we´re over at
the end of this year.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
I say it every single year,
and it never happens.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can´t believe people aren´t
sick of me yet.

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:57.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I --
-[ Laughing ] It´s crazy.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:00.026
-Not only am I not sick of you,
but, you know, you are sort of

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
the connective tissue --
Meredith Grey´s

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
connective tissue
of that entire show.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, what do you think it is
about the relationship

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
the audience has with
that character that they´re

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:10.236
still so engaged with her
fourteen seasons into it?

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I -- Maybe they´re
all drinking tequila.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.740
and not really paying attention.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:17.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, they´re paying attention.
-I don´t know, honestly!

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don´t know.
I think --

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:22.782 size:81% position:41%
I hope that, you know,
as actors our goal is

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.017
to make people feel, right?

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:26.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-And so, I think, you know,

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:29.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do my best to try
to make people feel something,

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:31.524 size:78% position:39%
whether it´s sadness
or happiness or anger

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
or whatever it is.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I do my best.

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.129 size:84% position:42%
And we all do our best.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it´s --
It´s actually, you know,

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:39.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
the journey of it has been
quite interesting

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:43.470
because obviously, we´ve had our
ups and downs behind the scenes.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:47.040
And I loved that we´ve --

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
the journey as a whole.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
It started out one way
and it´s ending --

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not that it´s ending,
but right now where we are

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:58.685
is such a different place
from where we started, you know?

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s been a very
interesting journey.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:03.656
-Well, I don´t think a show
could successfully succeed

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.758 size:78% position:39%
for fourteen seasons
unless it did change.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:06.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And was that something

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.495
that everybody understood?

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:11.197
Or were there people within
the production that thought,

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.199
"Oh, no, we can never change
this, got to stay this forever."

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:15.869
Or was everybody sort of open to
the idea of letting it evolve?

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:18.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no one´s open
to letting it evolve.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:21.274 size:88% position:44%
I think that, you know,
everybody was devastated

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
when Patrick Dempsey left.
-Uh-huh.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:26.980
-And I think that, you know,
the network especially thought,

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, the show was never
going to make it.

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:30.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they rushed in
a new love interest,

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.885
like, thirty seconds later.

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:33.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:36.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I --
I could never carry the show.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:37.790 size:75% position:38%
Let´s not get crazy.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, no, I think you could.
-I think Grey

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.927 size:78% position:39%
could carry the show.

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:45.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, no, it´s --
I think that now people

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:50.136
understand that the evolution
is part of why it sustains.

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:54.274
But I think that the idea of
something so successful changing

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:55.341
is frightening to people.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think change is
frightening to people.

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:59.979
-Your relationship with the show
has changed as well because now

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
you´re not only
an actor on the show,

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:03.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you´ve also
directed episodes.

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:06.653
How is it to see, you know,
a product you´ve been a part of

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:08.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
from one perspective
for so long,

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
how crazy is it to look at it
from a different side

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:13.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the camera?
-I mean, I really think every

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:14.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
actor should direct,
because it is

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:18.298 size:81% position:41%
a completely different
viewpoint, you know?

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:20.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
But again, I´m super blessed
because I -- You know,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
Shonda Rhimes has allowed me
to evolve with the show

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:26.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
and direct
and help produce the show.

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.975
So, now I have more ownership
over the show and much more

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
of a say.

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.177 size:88% position:44%
Did you ever see that --

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.879
The documentary about Bob Evans?

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
-The kid stays in the picture

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:37.884
when he says, the --
He says, "I want to be that guy,

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
the producer,
´cause I can´t get fired."

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:41.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:44.123
And I -- That always stuck
with me and I always saw that

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:46.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-- You know, you got to own it
and be a part of it

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:48.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause actors are sort of
the highest paid

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:51.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the totem pole, but
the lowest in terms of power.

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:53.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. They never kill off
the producer.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, they never kill off
the producer.

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:58.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, to have --
actually be a woman

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:03.009
in the television business
and have power over my situation

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:06.346
and for Shonda to sort of see me
as a partner instead of just

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:09.449
an employee is something I think
we´re both very proud of.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:12.685
-And I think that speaks
to how women in power lead

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
to more women in power
in any industries,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it´s really nice
to have Shonda there

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:17.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it´s really nice
to have you here.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.225
And congratulations on 300
episodes, what a pleasure.

